* wizslow - switch the module and the FPGA UART back to 115200 baud (undo wizfast).
* Needs: wizi, no connections active. ALL five devices go back: /wz bau=0 and
* /wz0-/wz3 bau=8 (packet flag only) - a packet descriptor left at bau=9 would flip
* the UART to 921600 again at its next open and go deaf against a 115200 module.
echo ATE1>/wz
modem /wz
echo AT+UART_CUR=115200,8,1,0,0>/wz
modem /wz
xmode /wz bau=0
xmode /wz0 bau=8
xmode /wz1 bau=8
xmode /wz2 bau=8
xmode /wz3 bau=8
echo AT>/wz
modem /wz
